# Subscribe to the SLPI's double-tap gesture, so it is reporting before anything
# needs it.
#
# The SLPI detects the gesture itself and reports it over SMGR; the kernel side
# is qcom_smgr's write_event_config(), i.e. this attribute, and nothing enables
# it by default. Without it the whole path is silent even when the SLPI owns the
# controller: the subscription is what makes it report, and it is accepted
# (sensor id 243, 1 Hz) but never implied.
#
# The other half is the handover, which the ftm4 driver now does itself as a
# drm_panel follower when the screen blanks. Both halves are needed; either one
# alone reports nothing.
#
# Matched on ATTR{name}, not iio:deviceN: IIO device numbering depends on the
# order the SSC sensors register and is not a stable identifier.
SUBSYSTEM=="iio", ACTION=="add", ATTR{name}=="qcom-smgr-double-tap", ATTR{events/in_index0_change_en}="1"
